{
  "comment": [
    "Byte patches applied to vanilla Far Far West Blueprints to make them work with 5-8 players.",
    "Offsets are into the .uexp of the legacy (retoc to-legacy) form of each asset; 'expect' must match",
    "the vanilla bytes or the build stops. Re-derive after a game update with kismet.py (see README).",
    "All but one patch are the same change: a Blueprint 'Select' keyed on the player count (1..4) returns",
    "its zeroed default for 5+ players; the default is pointed at the 4-player value instead. A property",
    "pointer in bytecode is [FName index int32][FName number int32], number N means suffix _(N-1).",
    "The other one widens the lobby's player list from 4 to 8 rows. Everything else (lobby cap, enemy",
    "scaling, gold magnet, colours) is done at runtime by the MorePlayers Lua mod."
  ],
